{
 "_comment": [
  "A2 \u2014 the spec-repair differential, complete. Two arms of `durable-approval-outbox` differing by",
  "ONE SENTENCE of agent-visible specification:",
  "",
  "    `ACKED` and `REVOKED` are terminal: neither has an outgoing transition.",
  "",
  "The control arm is byte-identical to the original task apart from its name (verified by diff -r).",
  "Both arms were built as fresh copies so neither is privileged as 'the original'. Free validation",
  "before any spend: oracle 1.0 on both arms, nop 0.0 on treatment.",
  "",
  "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS IN THE REPOSITORY. Phase 3's control set and probe lived in a scratch",
  "directory and did not survive a machine restart; only the numbers in its report survived, and one",
  "of them turned out to be wrong. Evidence that lives only in a report is a claim, not evidence.",
  "",
  "EXCLUSIONS are mechanical and are recorded below with the marker file that carries the reason.",
  "A run whose harness raised is not evidence about a subject \u2014 with one exception that is part of",
  "the task's own contract: `task.toml` declares `timeout_sec = 7200.0` for the agent, so exhausting",
  "that budget is failing the task, not the harness failing the subject. `AgentTimeoutError` counts;",
  "`NetworkConnectionError` does not. The rule is the exception TYPE, never the cost, because",
  "excluding on cost is a judgement made case by case in whichever direction the author prefers.",
  "",
  "VERSION CONFOUNDS. The 2026-08 runs behind the original 6/6 used codex 0.149.1; A2 used 0.152.1,",
  "so nothing here is comparable to that result. Within A2, `a2-control-opus-2b` ran claude-code",
  "2.1.259 where the other five Anthropic runs ran 2.1.258 \u2014 a patch release, on the control arm,",
  "which had the LOWER pass rate, so it cannot manufacture the reported effect."
 ],
